---

### 6. MEMORY MANAGEMENT CHECKLIST

#### Disposal Requirements (Explicit `.dispose()` calls)
- [ ] All `Geometry` instances when entity destroyed
- [ ] All `Material` instances when no longer needed
- [ ] All `Texture`/`CanvasTexture` instances after use
- [ ] All `Light` instances on scene cleanup
- [ ] `InstancedMesh` disposed and recreated between levels

#### Pooling Requirements (Zero GC Pressure)
- [ ] Bullet pool: capacity 20
- [ ] Bomb pool: capacity 15
- [ ] Particle pool: capacity 500 (hard cap)
- [ ] FloatingText pool: capacity 30
- [ ] ShockwaveRing pool: capacity 10

#### Level Transition Cleanup
```javascript
function resetLevel() {
    // Dispose old instanced mesh
    invaderMesh.dispose();

    // Clear all active entities from pools
    bulletPool.releaseAll();
    bombPool.releaseAll();
    particleManager.clearAll();

    // Reset scene children
    scene.children.forEach(child => {
        if (child.geometry) child.geometry.dispose();
        if (child.material) child.material.dispose();
    });
    scene.clear();
}
```

---

### 7. AUDIO SYNTHESIS SPECIFICATION

#### SFX Library (`SFXSynth.js`)
| Sound | Type | Frequency/Pattern | Duration |
|-------|------|-------------------|----------|
| Player Shot | Square wave sweep | 800Hz → 400Hz | 100ms |
| Invader Death | Noise burst + decay | White noise, exponential fade | 200ms |
| Bomb Hit | Low sine + distortion | 150Hz with harmonics | 300ms |
| Power-up Collect | High sine arpeggio | C6-E6-G6 ascending | 150ms |
| UFO Flyby | FM synthesis glide | 2000Hz → 400Hz | 2000ms |
| Level Complete | Major chord progression | C4-E4-G4-C5 | 1500ms |

#### Background Music (`MusicGenerator.js`)
- **Style:** Synthwave arpeggios with driving bassline
- **Tempo:** 120 BPM, increases by 5% each level
- **Structure:** 8-bar loop with evolving layers
- **Oscillators:** Sawtooth for leads, square for bass, triangle for pads

---

### 8. PERFORMANCE BUDGET & OPTIMIZATION TARGETS

| Metric | Target | Measurement Method |
|--------|--------|-------------------|
| Frame Time | <16ms (60 FPS) | `performance.now()` delta tracking |
| Draw Calls | <50 per frame | Three.js renderer.info.drawCalls |
| Active Particles | ≤500 | ParticleManager.activeParticles.length |
| Memory Usage | <200MB heap | Chrome DevTools Performance tab |
| GC Pauses | <5ms average | DevTools Memory timeline |

#### Optimization Techniques Applied
1. **InstancedMesh** for invader grid (single draw call for 50 meshes)
2. **Object Pooling** eliminates runtime allocation for bullets, particles
3. **Geometry Reuse** via GeometryPool for common shapes
4. **Texture Atlasing** for ship textures where possible
5. **LOD System** for distant starfield points

---

### 9. EDGE CASES & ERROR HANDLING

#### Input Edge Cases
- [ ] Gamepad connected mid-game → hot-swap to gamepad input
- [ ] Gamepad disconnected → fallback to keyboard
- [ ] Multiple keys pressed simultaneously → prioritize last input
- [ ] Rapid fire spamming → cooldown prevents queue buildup

#### Collision Edge Cases
- [ ] Bullet hits two invaders at once → destroy both, bullet consumed
- [ ] Invader dies while shooting bomb → bomb still active
- [ ] Player at screen edge when invader reaches bottom → game over regardless

#### Performance Edge Cases
- [ ] All 50 invaders die simultaneously → particle cap prevents crash
- [ ] Rapid UFO kills → floating text pool limits on-screen count
- [ ] Browser tab inactive → TimeManager pauses delta accumulation

---

### 10. TESTING CHECKLIST (Pre-Delivery)

#### Functional Tests
- [ ] Player moves left/right smoothly with keyboard
- [ ] Player moves left/right smoothly with gamepad
- [ ] Shooting has correct cooldown timing
- [ ] Invaders move in grid formation correctly
- [ ] Invaders descend and reverse at screen edges
- [ ] Collision detection works for all entity pairs
- [ ] Scoring updates correctly on kills
- [ ] Level progression triggers after clearing wave
- [ ] Game over condition triggers appropriately
- [ ] Pause/resume functionality works

#### VFX Tests
- [ ] Bloom glow visible on emissive surfaces
- [ ] Camera shake occurs on impacts
- [ ] Hit-stop freezes frame on boss kill
- [ ] Particle bursts spawn at correct locations
- [ ] Motion trails follow fast projectiles
- [ ] Shockwave rings expand and fade properly
- [ ] Floating text rises and disappears

#### Performance Tests
- [ ] Frame rate stays above 55 FPS during chaos
- [ ] Memory usage stable after 5+ minutes gameplay
- [ ] No console errors or warnings
- [ ] Particle count never exceeds 500

---

## PLAN COMPLETE — Awaiting Approval

