# STEP 2: Planning Phase — Space Invaders AAA Reimagining

## `plan.md` — Space Invaders Architectural Blueprint

---

### 1. CORE GAMEPLAY MECHANICS (Mathematical Model)

#### Player Controller
- **Position:** Constrained to bottom plane (`y = -8`, `z = 0`)
- **Movement:** Linear interpolation along x-axis, clamped to viewport bounds
- **Velocity:** `playerSpeed = 12 units/second` with input-based acceleration
- **Shooting:** Cooldown timer `fireRate = 400ms`; projectile velocity `bulletSpeed = 80 units/second`

#### Invader Grid System
- **Formation:** 5 rows × 10 columns (50 invaders total per wave)
- **Grid Spacing:** Horizontal gap `2.5 units`, vertical gap `1.8 units`
- **Movement Pattern:** 
  - Oscillate left/right at speed `invaderSpeed = base + (rowsDestroyed * acceleration)`
  - When edge reached, all invaders shift down by `dropDistance = 1.5 units` and reverse direction
  - Speed increases as population decreases: `currentSpeed = baseSpeed * (1 + (1 - remaining/total))`

#### Collision Detection System
- **AABB Bounding Boxes:** All entities use axis-aligned bounding boxes for collision
- **Bullet-Invader:** Simple AABB overlap check; bullet destroyed, invader scored
- **Bomb-Player:** Same check; player loses life/shield
- **Invader-Player:** Invader reaches bottom plane = instant game over

#### Scoring Mathematics
| Invader Type | Row | Points | Color (Hex) |
|--------------|-----|--------|-------------|
| Squid | 1-2 | 30 | #FF6B9D |
| Crab | 3-4 | 20 | #4ECDC4 |
| Octopus | 5 | 10 | #FFE66D |

- **UFO Bonus:** Random appearance, worth 100/200/300 points based on direction
- **Combo Multiplier:** Consecutive kills without being hit increase multiplier up to 3x
- **Level Progression:** Each cleared wave increases invader base speed by 15%

#### Game States
```
MENU → PLAYING ↔ PAUSED → GAME_OVER (→ MENU)
              ↓
           LEVEL_COMPLETE (→ PLAYING next level)
```

---

### 2. MODERN AAA ENHANCEMENTS (18 Specific Upgrades)

| # | Enhancement | Three.js Implementation Detail |
|---|-------------|-------------------------------|
| 1 | **Neon Emissive Ships** | `MeshStandardMaterial` with custom emissive maps generated via Canvas API; each ship type has unique glow pattern |
| 2 | **Dynamic Bloom Intensity** | `UnrealBloomPass.strength` scales from 1.2 (calm) to 2.0 (chaos) based on active entities |
| 3 | **Procedural Starfield Parallax** | 5 depth layers of stars moving at different speeds; created via `Points` with custom shader material |
| 4 | **Laser Trail Ribbons** | `MotionTrails` system creates fading ribbon geometry following bullet trajectory |
| 5 | **Explosion Particle Bursts** | 30-50 particles per invader death; velocity cone spread, gravity simulation, alpha decay |
| 6 | **Screen Shake Trauma System** | `CameraShake` accumulates "trauma" value on impacts; decays exponentially over time |
| 7 | **Hit-Stop Frame Freeze** | On boss/UFO kill: freeze `TimeManager.delta = 0` for 8 frames, then resume |
| 8 | **Shockwave Rings** | Expanding torus geometry with emissive material; spawned at explosion centers |
| 9 | **Floating Damage Text** | 3D sprites (`SpriteMaterial`) rising and fading; color-coded by point value |
| 10 | **Progressive Color Shift** | Scene ambient light shifts from blue → purple → red as invader count decreases |
| 11 | **Threat Flash Indicators** | Invaders flash white rapidly when about to fire bomb (0.3s warning) |
| 12 | **Power-up System** | Random drop on invader death: SpreadShot, Shield, RapidFire, HealthPack |
| 13 | **Spread Shot Upgrade** | Fires 3 bullets in fan pattern (-15°, 0°, +15°) |
| 14 | **Shield Barrier** | Rotating energy dome around player; blocks one bomb hit |
| 15 | **Rapid Fire Upgrade** | Reduces fire cooldown from 400ms to 200ms |
| 16 | **Dynamic Background Pulse** | Starfield brightness pulses in sync with background music tempo |
| 17 | **Score Combo Counter** | Visual counter showing current multiplier; animates on increase |
| 18 | **Boss Invader (Level 5+)** | Large multi-hitpoint invader at center of wave; requires 10 hits to destroy |

---

### 3. GRAPHICS PIPELINE CONFIGURATION

#### Scene Setup
```javascript
scene = new THREE.Scene();
scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x0a0a1a); // Deep space blue-black
scene.fog = new THREE.FogExp2(0x0a0a1a, 0.015); // Distance fog for depth
```

#### Camera Configuration
- **Type:** `PerspectiveCamera`
- **FOV:** 75° (wider for arcade feel)
- **Position:** `(0, 0, 25)` looking at origin
- **Near/Far:** 0.1 / 100

#### Lighting Setup
```javascript
// Ambient base glow
ambientLight = new THREE.AmbientLight(0x445566, 0.4);

// Directional for ship shading
directionalLight = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 0.8);
directionalLight.position.set(10, 20, 10);

// Point lights for dynamic glow (attached to ships)
playerGlow = new THREE.PointLight(0x00ffff, 1, 15);
```

#### EffectComposer Post-Processing Stack
```javascript
composer = new EffectComposer(renderer);
composer.addPass(new RenderPass(scene, camera));

// Bloom Pass - tuned for neon without washout
bloomPass = new UnrealBloomPass(
    new THREE.Vector2(canvasWidth, canvasHeight),
    strength: 1.5,      // Base glow intensity
    radius: 0.45,       // Tight glow spread
    threshold: 0.85     // Only bright surfaces emit
);
composer.addPass(bloomPass);

// Optional: Scanline pass for retro CRT effect (subtle)
scanlinePass = new ShaderPass(ScanlineShader);
scanlinePass.uniforms['opacity'].value = 0.1;
composer.addPass(scanlinePass);
```

#### Procedural Texture Generation (Canvas API)
- **Player Ship:** Triangle fuselage with cockpit detail, engine glow
- **Invader Types:** Pixel-art style sprites rendered to canvas, converted to texture
- **Power-ups:** Glowing orbs with type-specific symbols inside
- **Background Stars:** Random point distribution on transparent canvas

#### InstancedMesh Usage
```javascript
// Invader grid uses single InstancedMesh for all 50 invaders
invaderMesh = new InstancedMesh(geometry, material, 50);
// Matrix updates per frame based on invader positions
```

---

### 4. VFX IMPLEMENTATION PRIORITY LOGIC

#### Execution Order Per Frame (during render)
```
1. Update HitStopManager → if active, return early (frozen time)
2. Update CameraShake → apply offset to camera.position
3. Update MotionTrails → record current positions for trail rendering
4. Render scene via composer.render()
5. Update ParticleManager → spawn/destroy particles
6. Update ShockwaveRings → expand/fade rings
7. Update FloatingText → animate text sprites
```

#### Camera Shake System (`shared/vfx/CameraShake.js`)
```javascript
// Trauma accumulates on impacts, decays exponentially
trauma += impactVelocity * shakeMultiplier;
trauma *= 0.92; // Decay factor per frame

// Apply noise offset based on trauma level
if (trauma > 0) {
    const intensity = Math.min(trauma, 3);
    camera.position.x += (Math.random() - 0.5) * intensity;
    camera.position.y += (Math.random() - 0.5) * intensity;
}
```

#### Hit-Stop Manager (`shared/vfx/HitStopManager.js`)
```javascript
// Trigger hit-stop for N frames
trigger(durationFrames = 6) {
    this.framesRemaining = durationFrames;
    TimeManager.setPaused(true); // Freezes delta time
}

update() {
    if (this.framesRemaining > 0) {
        this.framesRemaining--;
        if (this.framesRemaining === 0) {
            TimeManager.setPaused(false);
        }
    }
}
```

#### Particle Manager (`shared/vfx/ParticleManager.js`) — 500 Hard Cap
```javascript
class ParticleManager {
    constructor() {
        this.maxParticles = 500;
        this.pool = new ObjectPool(Particle, this.maxParticles);
        this.activeParticles = [];
    }

    spawnBurst(position, count, type) {
        // Priority check: if at cap, remove lowest priority particles
        while (this.activeParticles.length + count > this.maxParticles) {
            this.removeLowestPriority();
        }

        for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
            const particle = this.pool.acquire();
            particle.init(position, type);
            this.activeParticles.push(particle);
        }
    }

    removeLowestPriority() {
        // Ambient particles removed first, then old trails, then explosions
        const lowest = this.activeParticles.findLast(p => p.priority === 'low');
        if (lowest) {
            this.pool.release(lowest);
            this.activeParticles.splice(this.activeParticles.indexOf(lowest), 1);
        }
    }
}
```

#### Motion Trails (`shared/vfx/MotionTrails.js`)
```javascript
// Store last N positions for fast-moving objects
class MotionTrail {
    constructor(object, maxPoints = 20, color = 0x00ffff) {
        this.object = object;
        this.positions = []; // Array of Vector3
        this.maxPoints = maxPoints;
        this.color = color;

        // Create LineStrip geometry for trail rendering
        this.trailGeometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        this.trailMaterial = new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({ 
            color: color, 
            transparent: true, 
            opacity: 0.8 
        });
        this.trailLine = new THREE.Line(this.trailGeometry, this.trailMaterial);
    }

    update() {
        if (this.object.velocity.length() > speedThreshold) {
            this.positions.push(this.object.position.clone());
            if (this.positions.length > this.maxPoints) {
                this.positions.shift();
            }
            this.updateGeometry();
        }
    }
}
```

#### Shockwave Rings (`shared/vfx/ShockwaveRings.js`)
```javascript
class ShockwaveRing {
    constructor(position, maxRadius = 8) {
        const geometry = new THREE.TorusGeometry(0.5, 0.1, 8, 32);
        const material = new MeshStandardMaterial({
            color: 0xffffff,
            emissive: 0x00ffff,
            emissiveIntensity: 2,
            transparent: true,
            opacity: 1,
            side: THREE.DoubleSide
        });

        this.mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);
        this.mesh.position.copy(position);
        this.maxRadius = maxRadius;
        this.currentRadius = 0.5;
        this.expansionRate = 0.3;
    }

    update() {
        const scale = this.currentRadius / 0.5;
        this.mesh.scale.set(scale, scale, scale);
        this.material.opacity *= 0.96; // Fade out

        if (this.material.opacity < 0.01) {
            return false; // Ready for disposal
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

#### Floating Text (`shared/ui/FloatingText3D.js`)
